### Start the API first: make up (Docker) or make db + make api-dev.
### Run the requests top to bottom: login keeps the token, create keeps the template id.
### Register ana@example.com first with http/auth.http (once).

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Log in: the token is kept for the next requests
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ana@example.com", "password": "secret-pass"}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### Create a template: 201 with a Location header and version 0. The id is kept.
POST {{host}}/api/templates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Language tutor",
  "description": "Corrects and explains mistakes",
  "content": "You are a patient {{language}} tutor. The student's level is {{level}}. Answer in at most {{maxSentences}} sentences.",
  "variables": [
    {"name": "language", "label": "Language", "defaultValue": "English"},
    {"name": "level", "label": "Student level", "defaultValue": "beginner"},
    {"name": "maxSentences", "label": "Max sentences", "defaultValue": "4"}
  ]
}

> {% client.global.set("templateId", response.body.id); %}

### My templates, sorted by name
GET {{host}}/api/templates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The template just created
GET {{host}}/api/templates/{{templateId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A placeholder that is not declared: 400, unknownPlaceholders = ["tone"]
POST {{host}}/api/templates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Broken", "content": "Answer in a {{tone}} tone, in {{language}}.", "variables": [{"name": "language"}]}

### Invalid fields: 400 with fieldErrors (name, variables[0].name)
POST {{host}}/api/templates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "", "content": "Hello", "variables": [{"name": "1st"}]}

### Update with the version that was read (0): 200, version 1. PUT sends every field.
PUT {{host}}/api/templates/{{templateId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 0, "name": "Language tutor", "description": "Short answers", "content": "You are a {{language}} tutor. Be brief.", "variables": [{"name": "language", "label": "Language", "defaultValue": "English"}]}

### The same update again, with the old version 0: 409 "This item was changed in another tab. ..."
PUT {{host}}/api/templates/{{templateId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version": 0, "name": "Language tutor", "content": "You are a {{language}} tutor.", "variables": [{"name": "language"}]}

### Without a token: 401 application/problem+json
GET {{host}}/api/templates

### Delete: 204 (409 with the configuration names if an assistant still uses it: see configurations.http)
DELETE {{host}}/api/templates/{{templateId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gone: 404
GET {{host}}/api/templates/{{templateId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
